            <ArticleTitle>Hemorrhagic pleural effusion due to pseudo-pancreatic cyst.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>42</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.4103/2277-9175.178789</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Hemorrhagic pleural effusion is a common clinical entity still diagnosis is often missed. An unusual and often over-looked cause of pleural effusion is an intra-abdominal process including complication arising due to pancreatitis. We report a rare case of massive left sided hemorrhagic pleural effusion in a patient due to pancreatic pathology.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
